# AUDIT — opm zero-trust (power-law 20%)
File: opm/audit/zero-trust.oot

Scope: this repo only. Date: 2026-09-04. Tag at audit: v2.11.1.
Working tree was clean on main.

Status: the kill list in section 9 is executed. See todo.oot
for landed vs blocked. The text below is the audit snapshot,
not today's code.

## 1. Verdict

opm is a real package manager, not theater. The 20% that works is
resolve, lock, caps, and the qa proofs. The CLI wrapper is dishonest:
help lists commands that main.oo never dispatches, and several handlers
still skip the first rest argument.

CI only auto-releases. scripts/test uses oodac check; if check exits 0
on ERR (current oodac), proofs can fake-pass.

## 2. Keep (the product)

- resolve/resolve.oo, graph.oo, pubgrub.oo
- core name/semver/caps; lock/; sign/; policy/caps
- qa proofs: today, pubgrub, semver, extract, ingest (they assert)

This is the unique move: resolve that refuses extra caps. Do not grow
more subcommands until dispatch is honest.

## 3. Kill or wire (dead / lying)

Help lists cat, git, io, more, pick. main.oo does not dispatch them.
Those files are helpers, not commands. Help lies.

cmd_more.oo is a compat barrel ("older cmd_pm_more imports still resolve").
Kill it. Do not deprecate.

cli/host_run.oo, host_build.oo, find_compiler.oo are copies of old ooda
build code. They still:
- fall through to bin/oodac and ooda/oodac_bin
- run sys_exec(sh, -c)
- export unused eval/repl

opm is not the compiler CLI. Kill the copies. Launch payloads through
OODA_COMPILER only, same as scripts/.

run_ooda_eval / run_ooda_repl: no main branch.

run_ooda_pm_sbom exists; main maps `sbom` to run_ooda_pm_audit, not sbom.

## 4. Argv (P0)

main.oo passes rest. Handlers that start at index 1 or 2 skip the payload:

- cmd_init.oo starts at i=2. `opm init myapp` becomes name "pkg".
- cmd_bot.oo and cmd_publish.oo start at i=1.

pm_arg_name in cmd_io.oo skips verb words. That is safer. Use it
everywhere. Do not skip by magic index.

## 5. Shell and ambient authority (P0 — Red 4)

sh -c in: host_run.oo, cmd_git.oo (git clone), cmd_reg.oo (curl +
minisign via command -v), cmd_bot.oo, registry/regs.oo.

cmd_reg.oo Setup says curl under SysCap. The function takes ProcessCap
and shells out. PATH hunt for minisign is a fallback.

No NetCap on HTTPS fetch. Fail closed: require an explicit fetch
primitive or refuse network.

## 6. Names vs function

| File | Name claims | File does |
|---|---|---|
| core/core.oo | banned generic name | semver + catalog resolve |
| cmd_cat.oo | cat command | catalog loader for add |
| cmd_io.oo | io command | argv/slurp helpers |
| cmd_more.oo | more command | re-export barrel |
| cmd_pick.oo | pick command | vendor picker; falls back to ../registry |
| host_build.oo | ooda build | compiler flags inside a package manager |
| docs/INSTALL.oot | VERSION file at repo root | RFC-0006 banned VERSION |

cmd_add.oo is 256 lines. Next edit must split it.

.github/workflows has no ANCHOR.oo.

opm/std is a symlink to ../std. Convenient; also a topology leak.

## 7. Ocaps

main takes FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. HTTPS and git use ProcessCap
as a stand-in for NetCap. That is ambient network.

cmd_init comments say SysCap; the signature has ProcessCap.

init manifest still pins min_pin=v0.210.0.

## 8. Tests

qa/ proofs look real. scripts/test.oo runs oodac check, not oodac run,
and treats is_ok as pass. Wire run once oodac check exits 1 on ERR.

CI: auto-release only. No test job.

## 9. Next five (this repo only)

1. Fix argv: init/bot/publish read rest[0]. Hostile probes first.
2. Make help match main.oo. Kill cmd_more.oo.
3. Kill find_compiler fallbacks and host_run sh -c. OODA_COMPILER only.
4. Stop sh -c git/curl/minisign. Refuse network without a real NetCap path.
5. Split cmd_add.oo. Rename core.oo.

Do not start more subcommands until 1-3 land.
Do not leave this repo for ooda/ or oodac/ without asking.
